/* A student record: name, class and total marks */
public class StudentRecord {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println("Name: Ananya Rao");    // identity line
        System.out.println("Class: IX-A");
        System.out.print("Total: ");               // no newline here
        System.out.println(78 + 82 + 90);          // arithmetic runs first
    }
}

// Output:
// Name: Ananya Rao
// Class: IX-A
// Total: 250

questions.prompt:
A student expects this program to report a mean of 83.33 but it prints 83. Identify the kind of error, explain why the compiler says nothing, and give the corrected program.
int total = 250;
int count = 3;
int average = total / count;
System.out.println("Average: " + average);

This program should print Hello and then 10, but it does not compile. List every fault, give the corrected program, and state its output.
public class Demo {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println("Hello")
        int a = 5
        System.out.println(a * 2);
    }

questions.answer:
There are three faults: the first println statement has no terminating semicolon, the declaration int a = 5 also lacks its semicolon, and the class’s closing brace is missing entirely, so the class body never ends. Corrected:

public class Demo {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println("Hello");
        int a = 5;
        System.out.println(a * 2);
    }
}

// Output:
// Hello
// 10
